      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ivan was formally established in 1908 as a logging camp, marking its transition from a forested wilderness to a working community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ivan_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Ivan post office opened on October 8, 1906, becoming the first official service that tied the scattered farm families together.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ivan_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ivan sits about seven miles north of Fordyce along U.S. Route 167, a stretch that later linked the town to regional trade routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ivan_arkansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "At roughly 213 feet above sea level, Ivan lies on the flat West Gulf Coastal Plain, making it ideal for early cotton and grain farming.",
